cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or computational framework, please cite both the software and the paper."
title: "Mitochondrial complex I dysfunction in idiopathic autism: convergence to a single chronic attractor and causal resolution by dynamic perturbation"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a bidirectionally coupled biophysical model of
  neuronal excitability and mitochondrial bioenergetics, including the
  phenotype-matching, inverse-problem, dynamic-discriminator (Table 4), and
  Sobol sensitivity (Table 5) analyses and LaTeX model equations
  (equations/equations.tex).
